WHY THEY EXIST, IN ONE SENTENCE EACH.  A decode request's query row was
`batch_idx` itself, which is true only while the launch's request numbers and
the plane's rows are one numbering; PIE's engine can hand these kernels a
plane a window sits inside, and prefill has read a `q_indptr` for that reason
all along.  And the cascade merge wrote its output dense from row zero, which
is the same assumption on the output side -- `win` is the `(count, start)`
seat every other kernel in this tree already takes, spelled here for the one
launch of the fa2 family that touches the fire's own planes.

