The table is a STEP FUNCTION, so it is total.  It returns a number for every
input, including a line that no longer exists and a citation that was never
written against the old numbering.  Re-deriving it independently -- `git diff
-U0` from `d737aad29` to here, an exact per-line map -- agrees with it on all
12,384 surviving lines, 0 disagreements.  That is the strongest check
available and it CANNOT see either error, because it ranges only over the
lines the table is valid for.  Two derivations of one quantity catch a
mis-measured quantity; they say nothing about a quantity measured over the
wrong set.  Read the table as: valid at and after each breakpoint, FOR LINES
THAT SURVIVED.  It is silent, not correct, elsewhere.

