Columns: guards, added lines, file lines, file bytes.

`bytes` is the fourth column and the newest.  `lines` alone is blind to an
in-place edit that keeps the line count -- change a constant, reflow an
expression, and all three of the other columns are unmoved.  A byte count is
not a checksum and does not catch a length-preserving edit either, but it
catches everything that changes a file's LENGTH, which is nearly every real
drift, and unlike a checksum it is computed identically by `wc -c` and by
`str::len` so the two sides cannot disagree about the algorithm.  The residue
-- a length-preserving edit outside every guard -- is what the network-side
check covers; `.wiki/driver/new-horizon.md` §23.8 records it being run.

AND THAT PARAGRAPH IS EXACTLY WHERE THE REGENERATION WENT WRONG.  The strip
of host C++ recomputed all four columns with a throwaway script, and the
script measured `bytes` as the length of the DECODED text rather than of the
file.  Rust's `str::len` is a byte count; Python's `len(str)` is a character
count; they agree on every ASCII file and this tree has two that are not.
Upstream's own comments in `attention/prefill.cuh` carry twelve non-ASCII
bytes -- em dashes and a `->` arrow, in `The SF smem layout is a plain flat
byte array` and three lines like it -- so its row was written 12 low, and the
totals row with it.  `xqa/mha_components.cuh` has two more and is not in this
table.  The row said 190667; the file is 190679.

It is recorded here rather than quietly fixed because the sentence above
promised the two sides *cannot* disagree about the algorithm, and that is
true only of `wc -c` and `str::len`.  A third implementation was introduced
to regenerate the table and it was not checked against either.  The columns
below were re-derived once more, reading bytes, and every row now equals its
file -- but the way this was caught is worth more than the fix: the per-file
removal ledger and a whole-tree before/after count were computed separately
and disagreed by 14 bytes, 12 in one tree and 2 in the other.  Neither number
was suspicious on its own.  Two derivations of one quantity are how the
defect surfaced, and the reason `f622dcf8d` stood for months is that nobody
had a second one.

